From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bepok <wojtekjakubiszyn@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:35:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: probe the MUSB gadget in board_usb_init

Without DM_USB_GADGET, gadget users find the controller through
board_usb_init(), which sunxi leaves as the weak no-op. Only
usb_ether_init() probes the sunxi-musb device, so with USB_ETHER off
the ACM console, ums and fastboot fail with "Controller uninitialized".
Probe the gadget device there.

Signed-off-by: Bepok <wojtekjakubiszyn@gmail.com>
---
 board/sunxi/board.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/board/sunxi/board.c b/board/sunxi/board.c
index 3d1afec7..b659e531 100644
--- a/board/sunxi/board.c
+++ b/board/sunxi/board.c
@@ -48,6 +48,7 @@
 #include <nand.h>
 #include <net.h>
 #include <spl.h>
+#include <usb.h>
 #include <sy8106a.h>
 #include <asm/setup.h>
 
@@ -866,6 +867,19 @@ int misc_init_r(void)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+#if defined(CONFIG_USB_MUSB_GADGET) && !defined(CONFIG_XPL_BUILD)
+/* Probe the MUSB controller for gadget users other than USB Ethernet (usbacm, ums, fastboot). */
+int board_usb_init(int index, enum usb_init_type init)
+{
+	struct udevice *dev;
+
+	if (init != USB_INIT_DEVICE)
+		return 0;
+
+	return uclass_get_device(UCLASS_USB_GADGET_GENERIC, index, &dev);
+}
+#endif
+
 int board_late_init(void)
 {
 #ifdef CONFIG_USB_ETHER
